// "Fight(a)" ([CR#701.14a]) — the bare-verb pattern TWIN: "whenever `a`
// fights". Fires per COMBATANT: the committed fact is per-subject, so `a`
// (the master form's `on` slot) matches whichever fighter's fact it names —
// either combatant, once each ([CR#701.14c]: a self-fight is one subject).
// Fight has no performer (`who` stays the defaulted Any). No second slot:
// no printed card narrows the OTHER fighter (no dead grammar).
(
    name: "Fight",
    template: "${0} fights",
    kinds: [EventFilter],
    params: [Predicate],
    body: Act(verb: Fight, on: Param(0)),
)
